.vercel
.env*
node_modules/

# ── 🔴 A CACHE AND EVIDENCE ARE NOT THE SAME THING ─────────────────────────────
# "A repo is not a cache" is RIGHT, and it stays. The line it draws is this:
#
#   A CACHE is regenerable and stays out. Anything one command can fetch or
#   rebuild again — a corpus reproducible from its manifest, a sibling page
#   measured as SERVED — is kept out of git, and the record of what was fetched
#   and when is committed instead.
#
#   EVIDENCE UNDERPINNING A VERIFIED-PASS ROW IS NOT REGENERABLE and goes in.
#   When the thing a tick stands on can never be fetched again — because the
#   live pages have moved on — its only copy is the one we hold, and a repository
#   that keeps only its hashes keeps a promise nobody can check.
#
# Ruling, beta-g as technical owner, 13 September 2026: THE EVIDENCE BEHIND A
# TICK MUST OUTLIVE THE TICK. So the 394 bodies the 12 September crawl captured —
# behind items 11, 42 and 48, in an Actions artifact that expires 2026-12-11 —
# are committed compressed as runs/crawl/bodies-2026-09-12.jsonl.br (659,647
# bytes). Their unpacked working copy, runs/crawl/corpus/, is a cache of that
# archive and stays out under the `corpus/` rule below.
#
# A NEW exception to "a repo is not a cache" must meet the same bar, in words,
# here: it underpins a VERIFIED-PASS row AND it cannot be regenerated.
# The 3,414-page corpus is NOT committed: it is ~200 MB of somebody else's rendered
# HTML, it is reproducible from corpus-manifest.json + the seed, and a repo is not a
# cache. What IS committed is the manifest (which names the exact 500 sampled URLs),
# the per-page CSV, and the written result.
corpus/
oet-corpus/

# The eleven sibling profession pages, fetched live for Gate A's denominator.
# NOT committed: it is 796K of ANOTHER PRODUCT's rendered HTML, it is
# regenerable in one command, and a repo is not a cache. Committing it would
# also FREEZE a population that is supposed to be measured as SERVED.
# runs/nursing-chain/chain-report.json records what was fetched and when.
runs/_profession-cache/
